From 90e23b42cb64de7b0d72051bc7dd2d9a47f5b24a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:11:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Candidate-set options: --sem_valid_grad, --sem_min_views,
 --sem_intervals

- --sem_valid_grad: Gaussians whose accumulated positional gradient is exactly 0
  are not semantic candidates (replaces the hard-coded condition; default off).
- --sem_min_views N: candidates must be observed in at least N valid views of the
  densification interval (default 1 = previous condition).
- --sem_intervals 3|2: 2 merges G2 and G3 into one interval (score < mean - 2 std).
- mean / std of the score are computed over the candidate set after these conditions.
- run_decisive.sh: VALID_GRAD (default 1), MIN_VIEWS, INTERVALS, DINO_CHUNK, GT_CACHE,
  OUTDOOR_IMG, INDOOR_IMG, ITER environment variables, applied to every arm.
- tests: new cases; resolve_sem_config test gets the missing sem_scale_mode field.

Defaults reproduce commit 343c470 (tests/test_decisive_cpu.py).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PHmjveU9kNqt1TKBUX99W4
